.TH XYNOOS 1 "November 2026" "Xynoos HyperCore" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
xynoos \- experimental read-only Linux resource intelligence
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B xynoos
.RI command " [options]"
.SH DESCRIPTION
Observe Linux counters on demand. No daemon or privileged intervention is
installed. Missing interfaces are reported as unavailable. Performance benefits
and physical hardware compatibility are not established.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B help
List commands and bounded options.
.TP
.B status, doctor, capabilities
Report observations and capabilities. Doctor does not verify package integrity.
.TP
.B resources --json
Report bounded hardware evidence and an experimental resource plan.
.TP
.B diagnose --count 2 --interval-ms 100 --json
Write bounded observations to standard output. Redirect to retain evidence;
the Debian build does not persist diagnostics automatically.
.TP
.B memory --interval-ms 100
Report experimental cooperative memory observations.
.SH PACKAGE MANAGEMENT
Use APT to install, upgrade, downgrade or remove xynoos-hypercore.
The update, rollback and uninstall commands refuse in Debian builds.
.SH FILES
.I /usr/share/doc/xynoos-hypercore/
contains lifecycle, security, licensing and build documentation.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR apt (8),
.BR dpkg (1)
